      "message": "This mechanism seems to be evolving and I don\u0027t want to change UAPI every time another change is needed. Let\u0027s remove reap_mem_when_killed_by and have this implemented as a vendor hook like this:\n\nif (!ret \u0026\u0026 sig \u003d\u003d SIGKIL) {\n  bool reap \u003d false;\n  android_vh_process_killed(current, \u0026reap);\n  if (reap)\n    add_to_oom_reaper(p);\n}\n\nThis way you will have enough flexibility to extend this further without UAPI changes until userspace reaping is upstreamed.",
